# 🛒 MaxStore MVC (BtoC) E-Commerce 
A modern, feature-rich, and scalable eCommerce platform built with  (ASP.NET Core + MySQL). Designed for rapid customization, and mobile-first responsiveness, MaxStore offers a branch of Myanmar food
 import from Myanmar for Kiwin people in New Zealand.

It is a simplified eCommerce version , specifically designed for ASP.NET Core junior developers and itermediate developers, using N-Tier architecture with MySQL as the database.
Since it is built on Entity Framework, you can easily switch to any supported database provider. For this project, I chose MySQL to accommodate the needs of my client. 
Front End User Screenshots
![MegaMyanmar Screenshot](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/maxzaw83/maxzaw/refs/heads/main/public/images/s1.jpg)



## 🚀 Key Features

- 🧱 Built on **GrandNode 2.3** (ASP.NET Core & MySQL)
- 🎨 Fully responsive UI with Bootstrap and jQuery
- 🛍️ Product catalog, variants, reviews, and filters
- 📦 Inventory & order management
- 💳 Stripe
- 🔒 Role-based access (Admin, Customer)
- 📤 Deployed on Azure (App Service )

## 💻 Tech Stack

- **Backend**: ASP.NET Core 9.0, C#,
- **Database**: MySQL 
- **Frontend**: Bootstrap, jQuery, Razor Views
- **DevOps**: GitHub, Docker, Azure DevOps (CI/CD)
- **Hosting**: Azure App Service

## 📦 Getting Started

### Prerequisites

- [.NET SDK 8.0+](https://dotnet.microsoft.com/)
- Entity Frame Work
- Bootstrap and JQuery
- MVC and NTire
- Node.js (optional, for assets bundling)

### Installation

```bash
git clone https://github.com/maxzaw83/MaxStore_MVC.git
cd maxstore

# Restore and build the solution
dotnet restore
dotnet build

# Start the GrandNode store
dotnet run --project MaxStore
🛠 Configuration
All settings can be modified via the Admin Dashboard 

Default admin credentials:

Email: admin@yourstore.com

Password: admin

⚠️ Remember to change admin credentials after first login.

✨ Customization
You can override themes and UI elements via:

Views/Shared/_Layout/

wwwroot/css/ and wwwroot/js/

Razor partials and layouts under Views/Shared/

📤 Deployment
Recommended (Azure )
Set ConnectionString in appsettings.json

Use dotnet publish to generate deployment assets

Deploy to Azure App Service or your preferred host


